WEBVTT

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:04.322
Ordinal encoding maps ordered categories to ordered numbers.

00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:07.772
The representation is compact and preserves rank.

00:00:07.772 --> 00:00:12.892
But some analytical methods may interpret the gaps between codes as equal.

00:00:12.892 --> 00:00:18.412
That is an additional assumption, not something guaranteed by the original category labels.

00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:25.602
Whenever you use ordinal codes, document the intended order and understand how the downstream model uses

00:00:25.602 --> 00:00:27.222
numeric distance.

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:33.227
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:33.227 --> 00:00:39.217
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:46.082
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:46.082 --> 00:00:48.320
floating-point number.
